<title>FRANCE: French consumer spending down 2.6 pct in Oct.</title>
<headline>French consumer spending down 2.6 pct in Oct.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>National statistics institute INSEE gave the following seasonally adjusted figures for household spending on manufactured goods in billions of 1980 francs:</p>
<p>					    Oct    Sept    Aug    Oct 95</p>
<p> Total				   58.14   59.71  60.67   55.09</p>
<p> Total change (pct v pvs month)   -2.6   -1.6    3.6	5.5</p>
<p> Retail sector			 38.14   37.01  39.22   36.52</p>
<p> Durables				17.70   20.34  19.34   16.14</p>
<p> Textiles, leather		   11.10   10.21  11.51   10.25</p>
<p> Other				   29.35   29.16  29.83   28.70</p>
<p>It gave the following percentage changes (month-on-month unless stated)</p>
<p>					    Oct    Sept   Aug    Oct yr/yr</p>
<p> Total				   -2.6   -1.6     3.6	  5.5</p>
<p> Retail sector			  3.1   -5.6     1.2	  4.4</p>
<p> Durables			     -13.0    5.2    10.4	  9.7</p>
<p>   of which cars		    -25.8   19.2    20.1	 19.1</p>
<p>   household equip		   -0.3   -5.8     3.9	  3.6</p>
<p> Textiles, leather		    8.7  -11.3     0.1	  8.2</p>
<p> Other				    0.6   -2.2     1.0	  2.2</p>
<p>INSEE originally said consumer spending fell 1.5 percent in September.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
</text>
